    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia**_\n\n**Before:** `TAB` stopped on every button: each title, then every TODO of every box.\n\n**After:**\n- `TAB` / `S-TAB` walk only the box titles (\"General agenda\", \"Thesis\", \"Issues\", \"Deadlines\", \"Config\", \"Notes\"), wrapping around.\n- `<right>` on a title steps into the entries of that box (its TODOs, or the rows of a menu block). `TAB` / `S-TAB` then walk only those entries, wrapping within the box.\n- `<left>` goes back to the box's title, where `TAB` walks the titles again.\n- `RET` or a click on a title still opens its agenda, on an entry it visits the TODO.\n- The key shown at the right of a title, `(a)`, is no longer a separate button (it is still clickable), so a title is one stop. This also fixes titles being two stops since the larger-title change.\n- Implementation: buttons carry `sp-dashboard-level` (`title` default, `item`) and `sp-dashboard-box` (the key of their box); `sp-dashboard--scope` holds the box being walked and is reset at each redraw. Doc and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n**Checked** (Emacs 29.3, headless): TAB over titles in order and wrapping, `<right>` into the General agenda entries, TAB and `S-TAB` within them, `<left>` back to the title; layout, privacy/Focus and clicking a TODO unchanged. **Not checked:** a real GUI, and entering a menu block with child rows (same code path, not run).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01T2BcMQ3qdNUiW5oZRLQRsG)_",
